import argparse
import hashlib
from pathlib import Path
import shutil
import pandas as pd

parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()
parser.add_argument('--antibodies', type=Path, required=True)
parser.add_argument('--hgnc', type=Path, required=True)
args = parser.parse_args()
O = Path('artifacts/paper_evidence/review_round4/protein_multi/corrected')
assert not O.exists(), 'Output already exists; preserve its frozen selection'
for name in ['sources', 'selection', 'prepared', 'evaluation', 'logs', 'runtime']:
    (O / name).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
shutil.copyfile(args.antibodies, O / 'sources/hao_antibodies.xlsx')
shutil.copyfile(args.hgnc, O / 'sources/hgnc_complete_set.txt')
annotation = pd.read_excel(args.antibodies, sheet_name="228 antibody panel (3')", keep_default_na=False)
assert {'#protein', 'Ensembl Gene Id'} <= set(annotation.columns)
assert len(annotation) == 228
annotation.to_csv(O / 'sources/hao_antibodies.csv', index=False)
(O / 'selection/rule.md').write_text("# Frozen RNA–protein pair selection and analysis rule\n\nThis rule is written before any imputation fit or imputation scoring. Seed: 1729. No selection threshold, antibody mapping, pair list, or split will change after selection is frozen.\n\n1. Use the downloaded GSE164378 3′ RNA, ADT, and author metadata files. Verify every supplied SHA256SUMS entry. Retain all author-annotated cells, including the Doublet category; apply no additional quality-control exclusion. Select at most 60,000 cells proportionally across donor × time × celltype.l2 strata. Allocate floor quotas and then largest fractional remainders, with lexicographic stratum order breaking ties. Sample without replacement using NumPy default_rng(1729); preserve source cell order.\n2. Count donors in the sampled cells. Hold out the two largest donors, breaking count ties by donor name. The remaining six donors are training (development). This choice uses cell counts only. Save every cell, stratum, split, and donor count before computing correlations.\n3. Use Hao Table S1, sheet `228 antibody panel (3')`, supplied with the paper (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/8238499/). Match its protein names to ADT names after replacing underscores with hyphens. Extract human ENSG identifiers from `Ensembl Gene Id`; cross-reactive mouse identifiers do not add human targets. Drop isotype controls, missing human targets, and antibodies with more than one human gene. Convert ENSG identifiers to RNA symbols with the saved HGNC annotation: prefer the approved symbol, then a unique previous/alias symbol present in the RNA panel. Drop missing or ambiguous RNA matches and duplicated RNA symbols. Keep separate antibody clones as separate pairs; disclose repeated genes in the summary.\n4. Normalize RNA by each cell's total UMI across all measured RNA genes: log1p(10,000 × count / total). Compute protein CLR as log1p(ADT) minus the per-cell mean log1p(ADT) over all measured tags, exactly as `sle_prepare_citeseq.py`.\n5. For each mapped antibody–gene pair, compute Spearman correlation only on training-donor cells where the original RNA count is positive. Keep the pair if this correlation is finite and at least 0.31, at least 200 test cells have original RNA count zero, and at least 50 of these test-zero cells have protein CLR strictly above the median across all sampled test cells for that antibody. The test protein enters only this requested feasibility gate, never the training correlation or fitting. Save all eligibility decisions and the selected list. Write selected_pairs.csv once, then freeze its SHA256 and this rule's SHA256 before any fit.\n6. Choose 2,000 highly variable genes on training cells using the existing `sle_build_fold.variable_genes` rule, (variance − mean)/(mean + 1e-8), with detection in at least max(5, floor(0.005 × training cells)); append every selected gene, preserving source order. Use the paper's 10% stratified nonzero mask (four gene-abundance and four library-size bins), restore every test cell's recorded counts, and retain only training masked-positive coordinates.\n7. Fit transductive gene-median, SVD (50 components), weighted kNN (30 neighbors), MAGIC (standard defaults), and scVI (standard NB, 200 maximum epochs, early stopping, L40S GPU) teachers on all cells. Fit the production boosted fused value and production MLP selector only on training cells, using unchanged repository scripts and defaults; selector on partition cs. No tuning. Safe Fusion ranking is its selector score. Comparator rankings use their standard output scales: count-scale SVD and weighted kNN, log-normalized MAGIC, normalized-expression scVI. Include scVI P(X>0), stored as the monotone score −log P(X=0) to avoid saturation ties, and log1p(panel library size) as a reference.\n8. Evaluate only original RNA-zero test cells, separately for every frozen pair. Spearman uses average ranks. Mean AUROC averages the 41 thresholds at protein percentiles 30,31,…,70, with strict `protein > threshold`, following the Papalexi evaluator. Hold the original thresholds fixed during bootstrapping. Draw 2,000 samples of cells with replacement within each test donor, preserving donor-specific sample sizes, using default_rng(1729) for each pair. Use identical draws for all methods and recompute Spearman ranks in each draw. Report point values and 95% percentile intervals for methods and paired Safe Fusion-minus-comparator differences. Undefined draws remain explicit.\n9. Report selected-pair count; Safe Fusion highest-Spearman count among six imputation rankings (library excluded; ties also reported); positive paired differences whose 95% interval excludes zero for each endpoint and comparator; median paired differences and exact two-sided binomial sign tests across pairs, omitting exactly zero differences. The pair-level sign tests are descriptive: antibodies may share genes, cells, and biological programs. Intervals condition on the two chosen test donors and do not estimate generalization across donors. No multiple-testing correction is applied; report nominal tests.\n")
source = sorted(Path('scripts/analyses/protein_multi').glob('*'))
dependencies = sorted(Path('scripts').glob('*.py')) + sorted(Path('src').rglob('*.py'))
for name, paths in [('source_sha256.txt', source), ('dependency_sha256.txt', dependencies)]:
    rows = [hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() + '  ' + str(p) for p in paths if p.is_file()]
    (O / 'runtime' / name).write_text('\n'.join(rows) + '\n')
